  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason: Character and Appearance\r\rOverall the proposed development is considered to be of a bulk, size and scale, which would not be subordinate to the existing dwelling and would thus harm the character and appearance of the existing dwelling. Additionally, the proposed architectural form of the hip to gable extension would harm the appearance of the symmetrical pair of semi-detached houses and therefore would not be compatible with the local vernacular and would detract from the visual amenity of the street scene.\r\rPolicy: In accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy, and the guidance set out in the Council's Residential Design SPD (2012) (SPD), development proposals are expected to demonstrate a high standard of design that safeguards the amenity, privacy, and outlook of both existing and future occupiers, while minimising the impacts of noise and air pollution. Proposals should also respond positively to the local context and, where possible, enhance the character of the area through a carefully considered layout, scale, and design that reflects the existing and emerging street hierarchy and built form. Furthermore, developments should respect and reinforce the character and appearance of both the original building and the wider surrounding area."
